_id\": \"server-4386c68c-edaf-cc95-3580-cfb3f67f774a\", \"leader_term\": 3, \"live_config_as_leader\": [\"server-3d56ac12-f394-7b79-8e93-c85ca99008ba\", \"server-6bc22c09-7a7c-8ab8-4990-ec4036ec805a\", \"server-4386c68c-edaf-cc95-3580-cfb3f67f774a\"], \"peers_leader_replicates_to\": 2, \"transfer_became_leader\": true, \"true_quorum\": 3, \"variant\": \"stale-smaller-config\"}\n11 {\"apply_error\": \"<nil>\", \"config_in_force_voters\": 5, \"derived_stale_quorum\": 2, \"event\": \"stale_config_write\", \"true_quorum\": 3, \"variant\": \"stale-smaller-config\", \"write_acknowledged\": true, \"write_backed_by_true_quorum\": false, \"write_holders\": {\"server-3d56ac12-f394-7b79-8e93-c85ca99008ba\": true, \"server-4386c68c-edaf-cc95-3580-cfb3f67f774a\": true}, \"write_holders_count\": 2, \"write_index\": 33}\n12 {\"acknowledged_write_absent_from_new_leader\": true, \"config_in_force\": [\"server-3d56ac12-f394-7b79-8e93-c85ca99008ba\", \"server-6bc22c09-7a7c-8ab8-4990-ec4036ec805a\", \"server-4386c68c-edaf-cc95-3580-cfb3f67f774a\", \"server-53e0296a-7a8f-a11d-c306-6a32ddd69790\", \"server-e91893d4-ea4b-1576-0d49-bd0ad3774608\"], \"event\": \"stale_config_loss\", \"new_leader_elected\": true, \"new_leader_has_write\": false, \"new_leader_id\": \"server-6bc22c09-7a7c-8ab8-4990-ec4036ec805a\", \"new_leader_last_applied\": 33, \"new_leader_term\": 4, \"true_quorum\": 3, \"variant\": \"stale-smaller-config\", \"write_acknowledged\": true, \"writ\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Read the retained receipt of experiment 161fc9455ca947cd80cc76048bf33653-experiment (CheckRun 1766eefaf1f14339ad1cff36e02a7c33, 13 parsed events): the stale-configuration chain completed and both comparisons were violated, so the safety account is raised from source-derived to a witnessed violations account and a behavior entry records the commit-rule consequence.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@k-stale-quorum-commit\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\":\\\"A node that leads with a configuration recovered from its snapshot while the configuration in force has more voters computes its commitment quorum from the recovered set: it acknowledged a client entry that only two of the five voters held, and a leader elected afterwards from the configuration in force (five voters, quorum three) did not hold that entry.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a commit-tracking store; the node restarts from a snapshot recording a three-voter configuration while the configuration in force is five voters and the recommitted entry is in its log but outside the restart scan; leadership of that node is then established and a client write is applied to it.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-commitment\\\",\\\"s-quorum\\\",\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"1766eefaf1f14339ad1cff36e02a7c33\\\":[11,12]}}\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"a867b593d52841198a36a897ae6a8f0a-question-1\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"161fc9455ca947cd80cc76048bf33653-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-commitment\\\",\\\"s-quorum\\\",\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\",\\\"s-runfollower-gate\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"1766eefaf1f14339ad1cff36e02a7c33\\\":[9,10,11,12]},\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account: the configuration gap makes an acknowledged write unsafe, not merely a stale local view. The receipt shows the chain: event 8 records the snapshot configuration as the three-voter set while the configuration in force has five voters; event 9 records the restarted node holding exactly those three voters (derived quorum two) with the log still holding a configuration entry beyond the snapshot; event 10 records that node becoming leader through the library's own transfer API with the same three-voter configuration and a replication set of two peers; event 11 records an Apply that returned nil while only two nodes held the payload, which is below the three acknowledgements the five-voter configuration in force requires, so the declared assertion 'the acknowledged write is backed by a true majority' is violated at index 11; event 12 records a leader elected from the five-voter configuration (term 4) whose log store has no entry carrying the payload, so the assertion 'the acknowledged write survives in the leader elected from the configuration in force' is violated at index 12. Mechanism from source: the restart applies logs up to the recovered commit index and the configuration scan then starts after that index, so the recommitted configuration entry never reaches processConfigurationLogEntry; the leader's quorum and commitment set come from that recovered configuration, so commitment.recalculate advances the commit index on the (n-1)/2-th match index of the smaller voter set, and both the leader's lease check and its replication set follow the same recovered configuration. The observation at index 12 is payload-based rather than index-based: the later leader reports last applied 33, the same index the acknowledged entry had on the stale leader, but its log carries a different entry there, which is why the payload check rather than the index is decisive.\\\",\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n    \\\"The state is reachable only with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled and a commit-tracking store, and needs a snapshot taken while a smaller configuration was committed plus later entries advancing the recovered commit index past the recommitting entry; a cluster that snapshots after every configuration change may not reach it.\\\",\n    \\\"Any later configuration entry or an installed snapshot repairs the recovered configuration, so the window closes once the node receives one; the harness prevents that repair deliberately by keeping the configuration stable and isolating a voter.\\\",\n    \\\"Both holders of the acknowledged entry were stopped for the final reading, so the observation establishes that the entry is absent from the new leader and not that it can never re-enter the cluster if a stopped holder rejoins; the acknowledged entry is nevertheless one that a true majority had not stored.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\n    \\\"Measured on one in-memory five-voter cluster with the repository's InmemTransport, InmemCommitTrackingStore and MockFSM; production stores, real network timing and concurrent client traffic are not covered.\\\",\n    \\\"The harness orchestrates a leadership transfer, a transport disconnection and the shutdown of the two holders, so the ordering is the harness's, though every step uses public APIs or documented test facilities.\\\",\n    \\\"A single run; the phase boundaries rely on bounded polling rather than on a synchronized schedule, and the reported holder set comes from scanning each node's log store for the exact payload.\\\"\n   ]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
